MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Step Back felt like a natural next choice because its blues guitar focus connects with what interested me in Memphis and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "The Breeze felt especially relevant after Old Sock: the Clapton connection and relaxed roots sound gave me a clear reason to choose it."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Every Time Two Fools Collide leaned toward classic country duets, while I wanted blues and roots rock; The Endless River's atmospheric instrumental direction also missed that mood.",
    "Soul City and 4.5 did not give me enough recognizable musical context to feel confident choosing them; that uncertainty does not mean I dislike their music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interaction with Blown Away seemed to lead too broadly toward country, even though country duets were not what drew me back this visit.",
    "A broad connection to established rock artists was not enough for me: The Endless River lacked the blues guitar and roots feel that made my strongest matches appealing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A direct connection to music I recently explored mattered more than a loose stylistic resemblance, which made The Breeze stand out.",
    "I rarely choose many albums at once. Rhythm & Blues, Old Yellow Moon, Bang Bang Boom Boom, and Boys & Girls could interest me without being compelling enough to join my two strongest choices today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in blues and roots music, but sometimes stretched that interest too broadly into country and atmospheric rock."
}
